{"name":"Nemophila","hex":"#a0a0ff","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Nemophila","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Boraginaceae – baby blue eyes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Nemophila"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nemophila","blocks":[{"text":"Nemophila is a genus found in the flowering plant family Hydrophyllaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Nemophila-menziesii-20080330.JPG/330px-Nemophila-menziesii-20080330.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nemophila","wikidata":"Q2738306"},{"title":"Nemophila (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Nemophila  is a Japanese heavy metal band formed in Tokyo in 2019. It consists of vocalist Mayu, guitarist Hazuki, bassist Haraguchi-san and drummer Tamu Murata. After releasing three singles between 2020 and 2021, Nemophila garnered a sizable multinational following online by uploading videos to YouTube. In June 2021, British record label JPU compiled the singles into the internationally released Oiran: Extended Edition. Nemophila released their debut studio album, Revive, in December 2021. Their most recent album, Apple of My Eye, was released in January 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Nemophila%28band%29_at_gramancy_theatre.jpg/330px-Nemophila%28band%29_at_gramancy_theatre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nemophila_(band)","wikidata":"Q109318109"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Hitachi_Seaside_Park_2018.jpg/500px-Hitachi_Seaside_Park_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Hitachi_Seaside_Park_2018.jpg/1280px-Hitachi_Seaside_Park_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp